15. Reaffirms that the measures renewed in paragraph 12 are not intended to have adverse humanitarian consequences for the civilian population of Yemen, nor to restrict civilian access to humanitarian assistance, commercial imports or remittances, and recalls the Committee's mandate to consider requests for humanitarian exemptions, to ensure timely and transparent decision-making, to continue to give due consideration to the humanitarian impact of the measures, and requests the Committee to streamline and expedite humanitarian exemption requests, including through a standing exemption for humanitarian actors where appropriate;
16. Requests the Committee established pursuant to resolution 2140 (2014) to continue its work, including consideration of the Panel's recommendations, and to report to the Security Council on its activities;
17. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.
